# Repo-root dirs that are NOT the site. Vercel CLI uploads the whole project
# (outputDirectory only selects what gets SERVED), so these rode along and
# pushed the upload past the limit -> "Error: Upload aborted" on 28 Sep 2026.
# content-writing/ was 6.0 GB of raw .mov reel recordings.
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING: gitignore semantics match an unanchored
# pattern at ANY depth, so a bare `references/` would also exclude
# website/references/ (the live hosted book PDFs). Keep these root-anchored.
/content-writing/
/whitepapers/
/specs/
/tests/
/test-plans/
/plans/
/mockups/
/design/
/docs/
/logs/
/patches/
/migrations/
/hooks/
/cron/
/issues/
/references/
/Formula/
/mlruns/
/scripts/
/src/

# /api/ is LIVE: serverless endpoints (stripe webhook, license validate,
# telemetry) declared in vercel.json "functions". Never exclude it.
# /node_modules/ at root is the api/ project's own install — leave it to the
# platform's normal dependency handling rather than blanket-excluding.

# Raw media is never a site asset (site images live in website/assets/img/).
**/*.mov
**/*.mp4
**/*.m4a

**/__pycache__/
**/.DS_Store
